WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.813
Chapter 11 puts it together
on one representative estate.

2
00:00:03.813 --> 00:00:07.320
It's a framing pattern, not a
report on a real engagement:

3
00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:12.387
the agency is a composite and the counts
are illustrative orders of magnitude.

4
00:00:12.387 --> 00:00:17.428
The archetype has about fifty thousand
users in two forests, one inherited

5
00:00:17.428 --> 00:00:22.712
from an absorbed component, joined by a
forest trust nobody documented or owns.

6
00:00:22.712 --> 00:00:26.752
About seventy thousand computer
accounts, twelve thousand groups,

7
00:00:26.752 --> 00:00:31.224
several thousand service accounts,
and about ninety SQL Server instances.

8
00:00:31.224 --> 00:00:35.663
The destination is Microsoft 365 GCC.

9
00:00:35.663 --> 00:00:38.388
Each phase ends with a
signed readiness bundle,

10
00:00:38.388 --> 00:00:41.113
and the next phase starts
only from that bundle.

11
00:00:41.113 --> 00:00:46.537
Discover: the read-only survey of both
forests, plus the service account scan.

12
00:00:46.537 --> 00:00:49.249
About four hundred accounts carry SPNs;

13
00:00:49.249 --> 00:00:52.288
about sixty rate critical
and a hundred high.

14
00:00:52.288 --> 00:00:56.802
Every SQL Server SPN is captured
with a pre-migration tag,

15
00:00:56.802 --> 00:01:01.413
because a missing or wrong SPN
silently falls back to NTLM.

16
00:01:01.413 --> 00:01:03.909
About ten instances raise findings because

17
00:01:03.909 --> 00:01:06.338
their service accounts
can't be attributed.

18
00:01:06.338 --> 00:01:10.913
Normalize: both forests have an
Operations OU holding different people.

19
00:01:10.913 --> 00:01:13.995
The agency builds an
organizational registry and

20
00:01:13.995 --> 00:01:17.224
resolves the collision there,
not by renaming groups.

21
00:01:17.224 --> 00:01:21.706
About two thousand users and several
hundred service accounts get findings,

22
00:01:21.706 --> 00:01:24.787
resolved by the governance
team, never auto-assigned.

23
00:01:24.787 --> 00:01:27.874
Map: an adapter contract for each surface.

24
00:01:27.874 --> 00:01:29.238
Four carry the risk.

25
00:01:29.238 --> 00:01:32.918
Sync, where cross-forest manager
chains decide the engine,

26
00:01:32.918 --> 00:01:36.599
since Cloud Sync doesn't
support cross-forest references.

27
00:01:36.599 --> 00:01:40.116
PKI and RADIUS, which move in lockstep

28
00:01:40.116 --> 00:01:44.200
because 802.1X EAP-TLS
depends on the same CA.

29
00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:48.612
And SQL Server, whose Entra
authentication needs SQL Server

30
00:01:48.612 --> 00:01:53.288
2022 or later and isn't supported
on failover cluster instances.

31
00:01:53.288 --> 00:01:57.087
Migrate: every operation is
a provenance-chained record.

32
00:01:57.087 --> 00:02:00.061
About three hundred drift findings appear;

33
00:02:00.061 --> 00:02:04.851
one P1 stops a SQL Server migration
until a role assignment is reduced.

34
00:02:04.851 --> 00:02:10.970
Validate compares the SPN inventories;
about three P1 findings are re-registered.
